## Session 3 — Bootstrap Prompts & Session Continuity

### Branch
`claude/new-project-setup-SJjFj`

### Discussion Topics

#### 1. Bootstrap Prompt for New Sessions
User wanted a single prompt to paste into a fresh Claude Code session that:
- Loads both `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` (global config) and project `CLAUDE.md`
- Discovers MCP config and CLI code
- Skips the discovery phase so the agent starts productive immediately

**Recommended bootstrap prompt:**
```
Read ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md to understand your full toolkit (agents, commands, rules, hooks, skills). Then read the project CLAUDE.md at /home/user/everything-claude-code/CLAUDE.md for repo context. I want to connect to Monarch Money - check the MCP config at mcp-configs/mcp-servers.json and the CLI code at mmoney_cli/ to understand what's already built, then walk me through what I need to set up to get a live connection working.
```

#### 2. Session ID Inquiry
User asked for the current session ID to hook into it.
- Short session ID (branch suffix): `SJjFj`
- Full session ID: available from browser URL bar (`https://claude.ai/code/session_XXXXX`)

#### 3. Session History Persistence
User requested saving full session context so future sessions can scrape it.
- Appended to this file (`sessions/2026-02-16.tmp`)

### Key Takeaways
- User is building a workflow where new sessions can cold-start with full context
- Sessions directory is the canonical place for cross-session memory
- Bootstrap prompts eliminate agent ramp-up time
- The `CLAUDE.md` files (global + project) are the primary context sources

### Files Referenced
- `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` — global agent/rules/hooks config
- `/home/user/everything-claude-code/CLAUDE.md` — project context
- `mcp-configs/mcp-servers.json` — MCP server configs
- `mmoney_cli/` — Monarch Money CLI
- `sessions/2026-02-16.tmp` — this file
